# Trivy vulnerability suppressions
# Each entry must include a justification.

# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — React Router RSC Mode CSRF Bypass.
# Applies only to React Router's RSC (React Server Components) mode. This
# frontend is a purely client-side SPA — src/main.tsx mounts <BrowserRouter>,
# and there is no SSR, hydrateRoot, StaticRouter or RSC entrypoint anywhere in
# frontend/src — so the vulnerable path is unreachable.
# No fix is installable: the advisory covers react-router 7.12.0-8.2.0 and is
# patched only in react-router 8.3.0, and react-router-dom has no 8.x release
# (it was merged into react-router in v8).
# Remove when migrating to react-router 8.x.
# Justification mirrored in .github/scripts/audit-allowlist.json.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
